    "body": "# Rung 0.3.1\n\nRelease scope: Rung 0.3.1 packages the free MIT-licensed repository\ngovernance-evidence engine for provenance-backed publication. This document\ndoes not establish that any registry or release channel completed publication.\n\n## Included\n\n- Eleven deterministic checks over public repository evidence.\n- Six evidence states: absent, claimed, detected, enforced, verified, and\n  unobservable.\n- A conservative maximum coding-agent authority recommendation.\n- JSON and text CLI output.\n- Reproducible verification receipts and independent replay observations.\n- A dependency-free standalone Python artifact.\n- A read-only GitHub Action interface.\n- Bounded, timeout-protected Git subprocess handling on Windows, macOS, and\n  Linux.\n\n## Limits\n\nRung does not execute code from the repository it audits. Public repository\nevidence cannot expose every enforcement setting, so those controls remain\nunobservable rather than being guessed. Rung is an assessment aid, not certification,\ncompliance advice, enforcement proof, or release approval.\n\nThe planned $5 paid report is not launched and is not part of this release.\nPublication of this release does not establish search indexing, usage,\ncustomers, revenue, or adoption.\n"
